7. Extrapolation attempt: median e_sym_gradient (shadow) vs depth
==============================================================================
points: {12: '7.7474e-07', 14: '8.8136e-07', 16: '7.0381e-07'}

linear   y = 1.0349e-06 + -1.7734e-08*depth   R2=0.1575 se(slope)=4.102e-08

log-linear ln y = -13.7237 + -0.0240*depth  R2=0.1809 se(slope)=0.0511   (x0.95 per +2 depth)

power-law  ln y = -13.2599 + -0.3039*ln depth  R2=0.1502 se(exp)=0.7228

Leave-one-out on the three depth points (log-linear):
  drop d12: slope=-0.1125/depth  crossing depth=nan
  drop d14: slope=-0.0240/depth  crossing depth=nan
  drop d16: slope=+0.0645/depth  crossing depth=87.4

Seed-band sensitivity: refit the log-linear through the d12 seed
extremes instead of the d12 median (d14/d16 have one seed each):
  d12=min: slope=+0.1618/depth R2=0.511 crossing=45.5
